#: docs/beans-and-todos.md:121
msgid "The prohibition is written here, and in the diagram's own documentation, precisely because the tool offers the operation. A rule that depends on nobody noticing a command is not a rule."
msgstr ""

#: docs/beans-and-todos.md:114
msgid "The reason is not tidiness. A scrapped bean records that something was considered and rejected, and on what grounds — which is worth as much to the next agent as the record of work that was done, because it is what stops the same dead end being re-entered. A deleted bean leaves a sibling session unable to tell abandonment from accident, and leaves the next agent free to start over on the thing you already ruled out."
msgstr ""

